{
 "about": "Reaper Master Series Paints triads: the three paints of each triad, as the maker sells them (shadow, midtone, highlight for a colour triad). Read by scripts/build-dataset.mjs, which gives the paints of a tone family their `family` and `tone`. Dev input, NOT shipped.",
 "source": {
  "publisher": "Reaper Miniatures",
  "url": "https://www.reapermini.com/paints/master-series-paints-triads",
  "captured": "2026-11-18",
  "method": "The page lists 76 triads by name and SKU, and no paint names. Each triad's own product image on the page (the `image` of each entry) shows its three paints, top to bottom, each with its code and name as text. The codes and names here were read from those images, in the image's order. Check: each code was looked up in the community source (Arcturus5404/miniature-paints, Reaper.md, which has Reaper's codes); 182 of the 210 codes are there, 168 with the same name and 14 with a longer or corrected name of the same paint. The other 28 are newer paints, additives and primers that the community source does not have, or codes that cannot be read. No colour value was taken from the images.",
  "rule": "A triad is a tone family (`family: true`) when all three paints are in the app's data as base, layer or metal paints, their Lab L* rises in the maker's order (a step may fall by 3 L* at most, because the hex values are approximate), and the hues of the chromatic paints are within 45 degrees. The other triads are sets of three products (liners, clear brights, coloured metallics, washes, additives) and get no family."
 },
